  "headline": "The quick tier (12 cells x 4 tasks x 1 repeat, 48 runs) detects nothing at all within a single cell - no effect size, however large, reaches 80% power on 4 runs, and needs 44 points for a main effect averaged over the other axis. A cell's rate can only take the values 0.00, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 1.00, so anything finer than 25 points is unobservable rather than merely underpowered. configs/full.yaml gives 99% power for a 20-point main effect and 55% for a 20-point interaction - the interaction is the binding constraint, needing four times the sample for the same size. Pairing across the shared task suite raises that 20-point comparison from 86% to 95% at no extra cost, since the same tasks run in every cell."
